§ `Regulation 34(2) as a prohibition (SHANT): traces, read by hand`

-- A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with #ASSERT on the main binary ("Trying to check equality on types that do not support it",
-- measured on 1.6.109), so these four traces are READ, not asserted.  Expected, from the text ("must not enter into, or continue"):
--   1. the institution enters into a relationship with a shell bank        -> BREACH
--   2. the institution continues a relationship with a shell bank          -> the "enter" rule stays open (a different act); the "continue" rule is breached (trace 3)
--   3. the institution continues a relationship with a shell bank          -> BREACH of the "continue" rule
--   4. nothing happens                                                     -> the prohibition stays in force (a residual obligation, not a breach)
-- The same duty is encoded as a decision function (`reg 34(2) the institution may enter into or continue a correspondent relationship with the other party`), whose tests are asserted above.
#TRACE `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution must not enter into a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution` DOES `reg 34(2) enter into a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` AT 3

#TRACE `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution must not enter into a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution` DOES `reg 34(2) continue a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` AT 3

#TRACE `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution must not continue a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution` DOES `reg 34(2) continue a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` AT 3

#TRACE `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution must not continue a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
